   364	## 6. Implementation constraints and deviations from PLAN.md
   365	
   366	- **G1. New members on pinned classes cannot be patched.** HookRegistry
   367	  resolves `getattr(owner, name)`, so the attribute must already exist. A
   368	  failure is logged and skipped, and `activate()` then raises "Hooks were not
   369	  applied". This affects the new methods in Q04 and Q09, the `_add_one_req`
   370	  split in P02 (a plugin function is enough there), and the dataclass/Struct
   371	  fields in F01 and T04. PLAN rule 3 ("copied verbatim") cannot hold for
   372	  bodies that call `self._store_kv(...)` and similar unless the framework
   373	  gains an `attach` declaration: set a new attribute only after verifying it
   374	  is absent at the pin, recorded as an "absent" fingerprint. The alternatives
   375	  are a class replace or mechanical edits that call plugin functions.
   376	  Orchestrator decision.
   377	- **G2. Zero-argument `super()`** in a copied method fails outside its class.
   378	  This affects E03 (`Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.__init__`), which must use
   379	  `super(Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding, self)`. That is a mechanical edit to a
   380	  "verbatim" body.
   381	- **G3. Copies run with the plugin module's globals.** Every private helper or
   382	  constant a copy uses must be imported into the plugin module, for example
   383	  `_TRTLLM_SPARSE_PAGE_SIZE`, `_get_best_config` and `logger`. Bindings made
   384	  before `HookRegistry.apply_hooks` are rebound to patched objects by
   385	  `_propagate_patch`. That is how copies reach other patched targets
   386	  (Q12→Q01/A09, Q08→A03/A05, T03→T02).
   387	- **G4. `fused_marlin_moe` is an eager custom op.** `register_custom_op`
   388	  defaults to `eager=True`, so the module attribute is
   389	  `torch.ops.sglang.fused_marlin_moe`. The copy must be registered under a
   390	  distinct `op_name`; reusing the name would silently route to the upstream
   391	  implementation (`CustomOpWrapper.real_impl` checks
   392	  `hasattr(torch.ops.sglang, name)`). `register_custom_op` itself cannot be
   393	  fingerprinted, because `fingerprint._locate` rejects its 5 `@overload`
   394	  definitions.
   395	- **G5. `lru_cache` targets.** The HookRegistry wrapper does not expose
   396	  `cache_clear`. Fork `test/qsa_hisparse/test_flash_attention.py` and pinned
   397	  `test/registered/kernel/qsa/test_qsa.py:162` call
   398	  `_resolve_flash_attn_varlen_func.cache_clear()`. With the plugin on, W4 must
   399	  expose `cache_clear` (and `_resolve_flashinfer_qsa_ragged`'s own cache)
   400	  through the wrapper.
   401	- **G6. Class REPLACE propagation (T04).** `_propagate_patch` rebinds
   402	  every module-level reference to the original class, including the plugin's
   403	  own alias. Define the subclass against an attribute read at class-creation
   404	  time rather than a stored alias. (F01 no longer replaces `ForwardBatch`;
   405	  see deviation D3.)
   406	- **G7. Unit tests with hisparse on.** The pinned
   407	  `test/registered/unit/managers/test_scheduler_chunked_req_gate.py` builds a
   408	  Scheduler without `hisparse_coordinator`, which S04's copy reads. The fork
   409	  edited that test (+1 line). W7's "installed but off" run is unaffected.
   410	- **Contradictions with PLAN.md:**
   411	  (a) Rule 3 vs G1/G2/G4/G5: some copies cannot be both verbatim and
   412	  activatable.
   413	  (b) U-list gaps: F01's `ForwardBatch` fields and Q05/T04's
   414	  `decode_score_width` match no PR; the log-level changes (U01, Z05) have no
   415	  PR; U7 should also list Z01's w13 `size_k` and gc changes and E03's
   416	  meta-device NGram embedding.
   417	  (c) The known hidden-change list includes the `shape_key` move, which is
   418	  pure (§4 item 3).
   419	  (d) PLAN W5 scope implies `moe/.../layer.py` is reproduced in full; Z05 (a
   420	  log-only line) is proposed as drop.
   421	  (e) PLAN says W4 handles "SM89 fallback"; the fork's fallback is SM86 and
   422	  SM89 (§4 item 5).
